gned}\n$$\n\nWe add this data to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $0$ | $4$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x+5-y=0+5-4=1 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot 1=1 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=0+1=1 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=4+1=5\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $0$ | $4$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $5$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x+5-y=1+5-5=1 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=1\\cdot 1=1 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=5+1=6\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $-1$ | $2$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $0$ | $4$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $1$ | $5$ | $1$ | $1$ |\n| $2$ | $6$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(2)≈6.$" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313796 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313797 13194139534840 true] [17592186313796 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534840 true] [17592186313796 1041 "field-1" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313796 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313797 13194139534840 true] [17592186313796 1110 #uuid "5e19446c-b0c6-5597-bd8e-6fa28231d437" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313797 1034 "6" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313797 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534840 true] [17592186313797 1111 #uuid "13ce50f2-2e13-505c-9061-5cddecd3b650" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313798 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313799 13194139534840 true] [17592186313798 1089 "q-351692" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313798 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534840 true] [17592186313798 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=4x+2y,\\,y(2)=-3\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with three steps of equal size to approximate $y(5).$\n\n$y(5)≈$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313798 1113 #uuid "8bf69a41-14a3-5531-887a-c43b607457a7" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313798 1145 "First, note that we are given $y(2)$ and asked to find $y(5).$ The distance from $x=2$ and $x=5$ is $3,$ and since we are asked to use three steps of equal size, our step size must be\n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{5-2}{3}=\\frac{3}{3}=1\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(2)=-3.$ \n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $-3$ |  |  |\n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4x+2y=4(2)+2(-3)=2 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=2\\cdot 1=2 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=-3+2=-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $3$ | $-1$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4x+2y=4(3)+2(-1)=10 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=10\\cdot 1=10 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=3+1=4 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=-1+10=9\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $3$ | $-1$ | $10$ | $10$ |\n| $4$ | $9$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 3.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the third row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =4x+2y=4(4)+2(9)=34 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=34\\cdot 1=34 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=4+1=5 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=9+34=43\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $2$ | $-3$ | $2$ | $2$ |\n| $3$ | $-1$ | $10$ | $10$ |\n| $4$ | $9$ | $34$ | $34$ |\n| $5$ | $43$ |  |  |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(5)≈43.$" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313799 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313800 13194139534840 true] [17592186313799 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534840 true] [17592186313799 1041 "field-1" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313799 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313800 13194139534840 true] [17592186313799 1110 #uuid "6838e483-7820-5f22-b04e-6d0e1b0169b3" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313800 1034 "43" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313800 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534840 true] [17592186313800 1111 #uuid "7487a604-95e3-5261-aec3-098f33a91bb7" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313801 1017 #edb/ref 17592186313802 13194139534840 true] [17592186313801 1089 "q-50091" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313801 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534840 true] [17592186313801 1100 "Consider the following initial value problem:\n\n$$\n{y}^{′}=2x+4y,\\,y(1)=2\n$$\n\nUse Euler's method with two steps of equal size to approximate $y(3).$" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313801 1113 #uuid "7d3d9541-c4d2-58db-87f5-eff80c4fcbe0" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313801 1145 "First, note that we are given $y(1)$ and asked to find $y(3).$ The distance from $x=1$ to $x=3$ is $2,$ and since we are asked to use two steps of equal size, our step size must be \n\n$$\nΔx=\\frac{3-1}{2}=\\frac{2}{2}=1.\n$$\n\nNow, let's proceed with Euler's method. We'll start by creating a table that includes the initial condition data $y(1)=2.$\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $2$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n \n\n**Step 1.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2x+4y=2\\cdot 1+4\\cdot 2=10 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=10\\cdot 1=10 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=1+1=2 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+10=12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this data to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $10$ | $10$ |\n| $2$ | $12$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =2x+4y=2\\cdot 2+4\\cdot 12=52 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=52\\cdot 1=52 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=2+1=3 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=12+52=64\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $1$ | $1$ | $10$ | $10$ |\n| $2$ | $12$ | $52$ | $52$ |\n| $3$ | $64$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n \n\nTherefore, we conclude that $y(3)≈64.$" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313803 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313804 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313805 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313806 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313807 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1041 "selection" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313803 13194139534840 true] [17592186313802 1110 #uuid "53ca2cd7-7f6e-555d-8826-70253ab0945f" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313803 1034 "