$ in the first row) and the values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x+y=3+2=5 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=5\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{5}{2} \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=3+\\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{7}{2} \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=2+\\frac{5}{2}=\\frac{9}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $5$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{9}{2}$ | $$ | $$ |\n\n**Step 2.** We compute ${y}^{′}$ and $Δy$ (using the values of $x$ and $y$ in the second row) and new values of ${x}_{\\text{new}}$ and ${y}_{\\text{new}}$ using Euler's method:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{y}^{′} & =x+y=\\frac{7}{2}\\cdot \\frac{9}{2}=8 \\\\ Δy & ={y}^{′}\\cdot Δx=8\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}=4 \\\\ {x}_{\\text{new}} & =x+Δx=\\frac{7}{2}+\\frac{1}{2}=4 \\\\ {y}_{\\text{new}} & =y+Δy=\\frac{9}{2}+4=\\frac{17}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe add this to our table.\n\n| $\\,x\\,$ | $\\,y\\,$ | $\\,{y}^{′}\\,$ | $\\,Δy\\,$ |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| $3$ | $2$ | $5$ | $\\frac{5}{2}$ |\n| $\\frac{7}{2}$ | $\\frac{9}{2}$ | $8$ | $4$ |\n| $4$ | $\\frac{17}{2}$ | $$ | $$ |\n\nTherefore, we conclude that  $y(4)≈\\frac{17}{2}.$" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313810 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313811 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313812 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313813 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1000 #edb/ref 17592186313814 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1041 "selection" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1104 #edb/ref 17592186313813 13194139534840 true] [17592186313809 1110 #uuid "b9b36b11-1994-515a-90ae-54a5da40dd35" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313810 1034 "\\frac{9}{2}" 13194139534840 true] [17592186313810 1103 #edb/ref 175921